             accessibility tree and tab order, so there is never more than
             one focusable "Contents" control despite two markup copies
             existing. First item in the group, before Scenes, per the
             brief. Icon-only below the row's full-label boundary, full
             label at/above it (global.css's `.nav-toc-label`, grouped with
             `.nav-scenes-label`/`.nav-chart-room-label`). -->
        <button type="button" class="toc-toggle nav-toc-toggle" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="toc-sidebar" aria-label="Contents" title="Contents">
